nodecode-magi is a rewrite of MarcosAlves90's MarcosAlves90/magi:
  https://github.com/MarcosAlves90/magi
  commit 3c08b45466c6d4c5f0047a24175c6734accb9c7e
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's memory workspace without its UI — a pending
queue of memory proposals read from the same records (one JSON object a
proposal under pending/memory/, carrying id, created_at, subsystem and a
payload of target, action, content and old_text, with add, replace, remove
and batch), the same MEMORY.md and USER.md entry format, and the same three
verbs a person uses on a proposal: list it, read it with its diff, approve
it or reject it. Approval applies the proposal to the store and removes the
record. As a cell rather than a Desktop page, the same verbs are also five
model tools and one slash command, and a proposal can be staged from the
conversation; the store and the queue are files the operator names in the
cell's section, so a Hermes profile's own queue can be reviewed as it
stands. Batch records are read and applied as their individual operations.

What was left out and why: the Desktop (React/JS) page and its dashboard
backend, the Electron interaction tests and the CI artefacts are UI and
build, not verbs. AI compaction, organization analysis and the second-model
preservation check called the Hermes runtime's model with structured output
and a schema; a cell would carry its own model plumbing and its own retry
budgets, so the rewrite leaves compaction as an ordinary staged replace a
person or the model writes. The profile-local Unix IPC socket existed only
so a separate Desktop process could borrow the Agent plugin's model; with
both halves in one image there is nothing to carry. The metadata-only
history log, the import/export JSON, and Hermes' native memory-store
safeguards (pinned matches, concurrent-writer recovery) are not carried
over either: the rewrite works directly on the two files and refuses rather
than repairs. Reading `store` from outside the profile is the operator's
choice, declared here.
